# One3D Checkpoint 1 API reference, in .http format for the IntelliJ HTTP
# client or the VS Code "REST Client" extension. These requests mirror the
# curl commands recorded in docs/evidence/2026-10-07-checkpoint-1.md; this
# file itself has not been executed through an HTTP client.
# Since Checkpoint 4 every request except the catalog needs a signed-in session,
# and state changes need the X-XSRF-TOKEN header. Sign in through the frontend
# (http://localhost:3000) and copy the JSESSIONID and XSRF-TOKEN cookies, or use
# docs/evidence/2026-10-09-checkpoint-4/real-stack/sign-in-and-security.sh,
# which signs in with curl. The API listens on 127.0.0.1 only.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@demoConfigurationId = 0d3d0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
# Paste the id from the Location header of "Place an order" below.
@orderId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### List orderable catalog configurations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/catalog/configurations

### Place an order for the seeded demo configuration -> 201 Created + Location
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productConfigurationId": "{{demoConfigurationId}}",
  "quantity": 1
}

### Read the order back (set @orderId first) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}

### Invalid: quantity must be 1 -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productConfigurationId": "{{demoConfigurationId}}",
  "quantity": 2
}

### Invalid: unknown configuration -> 422 CONFIGURATION_NOT_ORDERABLE
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productConfigurationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000",
  "quantity": 1
}

### Unknown order -> 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Checkpoints 2-3: production with the simulated printer (docker compose up -d db simulator).
# Start the API with: ./mvnw spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=demo
# These mirror the curl steps in docs/evidence/2026-10-09-checkpoint-2.md;
# paste the ids from each response into the variables below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@printerId = 0d3d0000-0000-4000-8000-000000000101
@simulatorUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8090
@jobId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
@attemptId = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### DEMO ONLY: confirm the order without payment (404 without the demo profile)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/demo/orders/{{orderId}}/simulate-payment

### Release production for a confirmed order -> 201, job RELEASED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ops/orders/{{orderId}}/release

### Record the start of the next attempt -> 201, attempt START_INTENT; RUNNING once the worker delivers it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ops/jobs/{{jobId}}/attempts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "printerId": "{{printerId}}"
}

### Simulator dev control (local only): the print fails -> observer marks the attempt FAILED
POST {{simulatorUrl}}/dev/printers/{{printerId}}/fail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "First layer detached"
}

### Simulator dev control (local only): the print finishes -> job AWAITING_QC, bed still OCCUPIED
POST {{simulatorUrl}}/dev/printers/{{printerId}}/complete

### Simulator dev control (local only): drop the reply to the next start command
POST {{simulatorUrl}}/dev/printers/{{printerId}}/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dropNextStartAck": true
}

### What the simulator's journal says about the printer
GET {{simulatorUrl}}/printers/{{printerId}}

### Whole-part QC -> PASSED accepts the job; FAILED needs a new attempt
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ops/attempts/{{attemptId}}/qc
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "result": "PASSED",
  "notes": "Whole part inspected"
}

### Operator clears the bed, naming the print that was removed (the printer's bedCycleAttemptId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ops/printers/{{printerId}}/clear-bed
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attemptId": "{{attemptId}}"
}

### Retry delivery of a start whose automatic tries ran out
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ops/attempts/{{attemptId}}/reconcile

### Delivery work that needs an operator
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ops/work?status=EXHAUSTED

### Mark the order ready for handoff -> 409 JOB_NOT_ACCEPTED until QC passed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ops/orders/{{orderId}}/ready-for-handoff

### Job with all attempts
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ops/jobs/{{jobId}}

### Printers: ownership and bed state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ops/printers
